# Build context for docker/service.Dockerfile.
#
# The image build runs its own `dotnet restore` + `dotnet publish` inside the SDK stage, so host build
# output is never read — but it is still *sent*. That matters more than it looks: the `Images` target
# depends on `Compile`, so the solution is always built before any image is, and without this file every
# one of the six builds ships a full copy of the solution's bin/obj into its context. Locally that is
# ~1.5 GB, six times over.
#
# Excluding .git is safe only because nothing here derives a version from it — no GitVersion, MinVer or
# Nerdbank. Revisit this line if that ever changes.

**/bin/
**/obj/
.git/
.github/
.artifacts/
.fallout/
.vs/
.idea/
**/node_modules/
**/.DS_Store

# The compose bind-mount target — media, never part of an image.
downloads/
